\noindent In forthcoming arguments, $\mathcal{A}$ is used to define the authenticated spaces of codewords, whether with finite or infinitely many bits, of Alice, Bob and Eve. Over $A \longleftrightarrow B$, and $B \longleftrightarrow E$, we denote such spaces of codewords with,


\begin{align*}
