\noindent Determining the circumstances under which resilient communication protocols can be enacted by Alice, and Bob, in the presence of Eve is significant for Information processing tasks. In providing arguments for obtaining one possible class of upper bounds on $r$, through the converse result which provides upper bounds on the bit transmission rate, Alice and Bob can realize proposed sources of Quantum advantage, albeit Eve's attempt to corrupt codewords transmitted between them. 


In the case of alphabets for each player consisting of a few letters, in the presence of a larger noise threshold over Alice and Bob's channel, in comparison to that over Bob and Eve's channel, the overlap function,


\begin{align*}
