\end{align*}




\noindent is represented as a supremum over all possible false acceptance encodings that Alice, or Bob, can use for accepting a message that has been tampered with by Eve. First, denote $\textbf{X}$, and $\textbf{Y}$, as the alphabets for Alice, and Bob, respectively. To discuss upper, and lower, bounds on the bit transmission rate, denote, additionally,

\begin{align*}
