\noindent Beginning from the conditional probability above, we repeatedly make use of Bayes' Rule, three times in fact, in addition to taking a supremum over the class $\mathrm{EC}$ of error correcting codes. By making use of the fact that the overlap function, $\mathscr{O}$, over $A \longleftrightarrow B$ is dependent upon the alphabets of all three players, namely $\textbf{X}$, $\textbf{Y}$, and $\textbf{Z}$, we obtain the desired lower bound, $p_{\mathrm{EC},B \longleftrightarrow E}$, by taking the limit of, 

