		(a) Non-monotonic behaviour of $\tau_\alpha$ as a function of $\tau_p$ at various $f_0^2$ and $\phi=0.65$. The lines combine Eqs.~(\ref{eq:VFT}, \ref{f0eq}) (see SM Table S1).
		(b, c, d) The dependence of $\phi_c(f_0^2,\tau_p)$ on $\tau_p$ for a small, an intermediate and a large value of $f_0^2$, showing a change from a monotonically increasing to a monotonically decreasing trend, with non-monotonic variation for the intermediate $f_0^2$. Lines represent the analytical description in Eq.~(\ref{critsurf}).
		(e) Time decay of $F_s(k,t)$ for $\phi=0.65$ and $f_0^2=0.045$ and various $\tau_p$. The intermediate time plateau at small $\tau_p$, i.e.\ in the glassy regime, disappears at large $\tau_p$ in the jamming regime. }
