We further validate our error model by using the breathing mode to mediate the entangling gate for the (1,3) ion pair. In this configuration, gate errors arising from motional heating and gradient crosstalk are significantly suppressed. Experimental results demonstrate a gate error of 0.028(1), in agreement with numerical simulations predicting 0.027 (see Supplementary Information for details). 

\subsection{Extending to longer chains}

