The  signals propagation time is also very much similar 
to the finite propagation of the physical fields, and even the latency time of the interfaces can be paired with
creating and attenuating the physical carriers. Zero-time on/off signals are possible both in the classical physics and classical computing,
while in the corresponding modern counterparts, to create, transfer and detect signals 
time must be accounted for; the effect noticed as that the time delay through wires (in this extended sense) grows compared to the time of gating~\cite{LimitsOfLimits2014}. 

