Hence we take $R=M\nu\sqrt{2r\log(2W/\epsilon)}$ and we assume the event in Eq. (\ref{eq:LoRA:bound}) holds in the remaining of the proof. \footnote{If we set $L^2$ constraints on $A^{(t)}$ instead of $L^{\infty}$ norm, the constraint size $M$ can be put inside the $\log$ to further improve the bound.} 


