    \eqdef 
        {B^{(t)}}^{\dagger}\,(\bar{I}_{d_{t+1},d_t} - W^{(t)})
\end{equation}
where ${B^{(t)}}^{\dagger}$ denotes the Moore-Penrose pseudo-inverse of $B^{(t)}$ (which we recall, is a right-inverse of $B^{(t)}$ if $B^{(t)}$ has full row-rank).

By construction, we have that: for each $(x,y)\in \operatorname{supp}(\mathbb{P})$ 
