 \linewidth]{%
    \includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{Tmaxm1.png}%
  }
  \caption{Illustration of Conjecture \ref{Conj:general} and Conjecture \ref{Conj:explicit} for sufficiently large $k$. (note that the scales of the vertical and horizontal axes are chosen differently to be able to depict it here). The graph could be locally concave or convex; our conjectures only claim that the graph is increasing, which suffices to conclude Conjecture \ref{1978Conj} in 3D and Conjecture \ref{necessaryCondition} in 3D and for tetrahedral numbers.}
