The codes we use are as follows. One of the most effective ways is to fix the colenght and also the number of (minimal) generators (from $2k+2$ to ${k+2 \choose 2}$) and list all the Borel-fixed ideals and the dimension of the tangent space at the corresponding point of the Hilbert scheme. In the following codes, we fix $\colength=35$ and the number of generators, $18$. The third line lists all Borel-fixed ideals $I$ of colength $35$ with $18$ (minimal) generators along with the dimension of the tangent space to the Hilbert scheme at the point $[I]$. 
