Similarly, the $\eta$-dependent flow harmonics $V_{n\Delta}(\eta^{a},\eta^{b})$ are calculated by constructing two-particle correlations between pseudorapidity bins $\eta^{a}$ and $\eta^{b}$, following the same method as Eq.~\ref{eq: Fourier 2PC} but replacing $p_{T}^{\mathrm{a}}$ and $p_{T}^{\mathrm{b}}$ with $\eta^{a}$ and $\eta^{b}$. In order to investigate the longitudinal fluctuations of the flow vector, the decorrelation ratio $r_n(\eta^{a},\eta^{b})$ was proposed in Ref.~\cite{CMS:2015xmx}, which is defined as:
\begin{small} \begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
r_n(\eta^{a},\eta^{b}) &= \frac{V_{n\Delta}(-\eta^{a},\eta^{b})}{V_{n\Delta}(\eta^{a},\eta^{b})} \\
                       &= \frac{\langle v_{n}(-\eta^{a})v_{n}(\eta^{b})\mathrm{cos}[n(\Psi_{n}(-\eta^{a})-\Psi_{n}(\eta^{b}))] \rangle}{\langle v_{n}(\eta^{a})v_{n}(\eta^{b})\mathrm{cos}[n(\Psi_{n}(\eta^{a})-\Psi_{n}(\eta^{b}))] \rangle },
\end{aligned}
\label{eq: rn_eta} 
\end{equation} \end{small}
where the $\mathrm{cos}[n(\Psi_{n}(\eta^{a})-\Psi_{n}(\eta^{b}))]$ represents the impact of the variation in symmetry plane angles between the $\eta^{a}$ and $\eta^{b}$ bins, resulting from the $\eta$-dependent flow angle fluctuations. In addition, the flow magnitude decorrelation introduces additional $\eta$-dependent fluctuations, lead to the break of factorization of flow coefficient products: $\langle v_{n}(-\eta^{a})v_{n}(\eta^{b}) \rangle \neq \sqrt{\langle v_{n}^{2}(-\eta^{a}) \rangle}\sqrt{\langle v_{n}^{2}(\eta^{b}) \rangle}$. For symmetric collision systems like Pb--Pb collisions, the $v_{n}$ obtained from symmetric positive $[v_n(\eta_a)]$ and negative $[v_n(-\eta_a)]$ $\eta$ regions are identical after averaging over all events. Therefore, the $r_n(\eta^{a},\eta^{b})$ is expected to converge to unity if neither flow magniture nor flow angle fluctuate along the longitudinal direction. If either of these effects, or both, are present, the $r_n(\eta^{a},\eta^{b})$ will be less than unity~\cite{ALICE:2023tvh}. However, in an asymmetric collision system, such as p--Pb collisions, $v_n(\eta_a)$ and $v_n(-\eta_a)$ are generally not identical. As a result, it is not possible to isolate the $\eta$-dependent effects of symmetry-plane fluctuations in Eq.~\ref{eq: rn_eta}. The CMS collaboration proposed a method~\cite{CMS:2015xmx} to take the product of $r_n(\eta^{a},\eta^{b})$ and $r_n(-\eta^{a},-\eta^{b})$:
\begin{small}
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
&\sqrt{r_n(\eta^{a},\eta^{b})r_n(-\eta^{a},-\eta^{b})} \\
& = \sqrt{\frac{\langle v_{n}(-\eta^{a})v_{n}(\eta^{b})\rangle \langle v_{n}(\eta^{a})v_{n}(-\eta^{b})\rangle}{ \langle v_{n}(\eta^{a})v_{n}(\eta^{b})\rangle \langle v_{n}(-\eta^{a})v_{n}(-\eta^{b})\rangle}}
\cdot \\ 
& \sqrt{\frac{\langle \mathrm{cos}[n(\Psi_{n}(-\eta^{a})-\Psi_{n}(\eta^{b}))] \rangle}{\langle \mathrm{cos}[n(\Psi_{n}(\eta^{a})-\Psi_{n}(\eta^{b}))] \rangle }  \frac{\langle \mathrm{cos}[n(\Psi_{n}(\eta^{a})-\Psi_{n}(-\eta^{b}))] \rangle}{\langle \mathrm{cos}[n(\Psi_{n}(-\eta^{a})-\Psi_{n}(-\eta^{b}))]\rangle}}
\end{aligned}
\label{eq: rn_eta_approx_pPb} 
\end{equation} 
\end{small}
In this case, the $v_{n}$ terms can be canceled in if there is no flow vector magnitude fluctuations, then the $\eta$-dependent flow vector decorrelation in p--Pb collisions can also be studied.

