\section{Experiment 1: G-SYNC Within Participants} \label{sec:within}

 Watson et al. \cite{watson2019effects} showed G-SYNC can improve gaming performance and experience in 30Hz frame rate systems, and found intriguing relationships between G-SYNC's effects and the traits of both games and gamers. We wished to study the same questions in a more PC-centric and future-proof 60Hz gaming context. To do so, we carefully designed a 60Hz PC gaming environment and introduced an implicit measure of experience, the Implicit Association Test (IAT) \cite{greenwald1998measuring}.


\subsection{Participants}

32 students participated in our experiment, all undergraduates or graduates in Computer Science. We recruited them using email announcements and compensated them with extra credit in their course or with \$10 Amazon gift cards. Table \ref{tab:Table1} shows how we assigned participants to different between-participant groups.

