\section{Conclusion}
In this paper, we propose a concrete optimization algorithm with provable convergence and generalization guarantee in supervised transfer learning. The analyzed procedure is a mixed-samples SGD approach that alternates between sampling from source or target data at an adaptive sampling rate. Both theoretical and experimental results show that our method is adaptive to whether the source or target data are most beneficial. This work aims to initiate the theoretical study of computationally efficient methods for transfer learning.

