\section{Limitations}
We acknowledge the following limitations in the study. As outlined by prior work, there are critical capabilities an AI system must develop to deliver effective apologies: abilities to detect the offense, attribute fault, explain the cause, and adapt future behavior \cite{mutlu2016cognitive}. Additionally, our investigation was scenario-based: participants imagined themselves as the wronged party. Although vignettes allow precise control over error type and apology content, they inevitably lose some ecological validity. We mitigated this by providing contextual ``sign-posting'' and by prompting open-ended reflections, and participants’ detailed answers suggest they engaged seriously with the scenarios. 

