      \field{abstract}{In this work, we study matroids over a domain and several classical combinatorial and algebraic invariants related. We define their Grothendieck-Tutte polynomial \$T\_\{\textbackslash mathcal\{M\}\}(x,y)\$, extending the definition given by Fink and Moci in 2016, and we show that such polynomial has the classical deletion-contraction property. Moreover, we study the set of independencies for a realizable matroid over a domain, generalizing the definition of \textbackslash emph\{poset of torsions\} \$Gr(\textbackslash mathcal\{M\})\$ given by the second author in 2017. This is a union of identical simplicial posets as for (quasi-)arithmetic matroids. The new notions harmonize naturally through the face module \$N\_\textbackslash mathcal\{M\}\$ of the matroid over a domain. Whenever \$Gr(\textbackslash mathcal\{M\})\$ is a finite poset, the Hilbert series \$N\_\textbackslash mathcal\{M\}(t)\$ of its face module is a specialization of the Tutte polynomial \$T\_\{\textbackslash mathcal\{M\}\}(x,y)\$. Further, for arrangements of codimension-one abelian subvarities of an elliptic curve admitting complex multiplication, we extend certain results of Bibby and we provide an algebraic interpretation of the elliptic Tutte polynomial.}
